# Build artifacts
bin/
obj/
*.user

# Local dev tooling - portable Postgres binaries + actual DB files, and
# the dev superuser password file used to init it. None of this belongs
# in source control; see README for how to regenerate it on a new machine.
tools/postgresql/
tools/pgdata/
tools/pgpass.txt
tools/pg.log

# .NET user-secrets are stored outside the repo (%APPDATA%), never here -
# nothing to ignore for them, just don't put secrets in appsettings*.json.

# Local file storage - the credential encryption key (secret.key, the one
# genuinely irreplaceable piece of local state - see AesGcmCredentialCipher)
# plus uploaded artifacts/catalog media once those land. Never committed;
# back these up (or the whole data/ folder) alongside Postgres dumps.
src/BandManager.Web/data/

# Docker Compose's bind-mounted app data (secret.key, uploads, catalog,
# branding) and the .env holding the real Postgres password - same
# never-commit rule as the dev data/ folder above.
/data/
.env

.vs/
*.swp
